#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119426 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e84e45ca-c250-5e65-a04e-4714a485f38e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Determinant of a Triangular Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "6a0257ef-3ec6-501c-bbf7-1c1108d4f8b6" :question/math-academy-id "e-10991" :question/problem "Calculate \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043085/assets/26dbd9a28532c3c262ca8015444364febabb8e269e5c6310a8fc59268f6e215c.png)" :question/worked-solution "The determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 10 & \\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 6 & -2\\end{aligned}| & =(-2)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\sqrt{3}\\cdot (-2)=4\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119427 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "02e65c73-8c02-5403-8c5c-b1e81f81a7b6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With Many Zeros"}] :question/id #uuid "c9760010-bcdd-53f4-8428-a3f5ecdd838b" :question/math-academy-id "e-10992" :question/problem "Find the determinant of the matrix \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043085/assets/28a22a5f860f02e42abc699e9807de885cc01b572c23ac0d4f909fe281042e08.png)" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the $1$st column contains three zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $1$st column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 13 & 19 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 13 & 19 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 13 & 19 & -3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 13 & 19 & -3\\end{aligned}| & =1\\cdot 2\\cdot (-3)=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\det(A) = 2 \\cdot (-6) = -12.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119428 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6a3d254-c96f-5aa0-9db6-a587eb7cb2de" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Expression Involving Given Determinants and Matrix Types"}] :question/id #uuid "1a6556a1-22b3-5e9b-97aa-d3e644df9f56" :question/math-academy-id "e-10993" :question/problem "Given that $\\det(A)=4,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\textrm{det}(A^T)=16$\n\n- $3\\textrm{det}(A^T)=12$\n\n- $\\textrm{det}(A^T)+\\textrm{det}(I)=17$" :question/worked-solution "From the properties of determinants, we know that \n\n$$\n\\textrm{det}(A^T)=\\textrm{det}(A)=4\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\textrm{det}(I)=1.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Rather, \n\n$$\n\\textrm{det}(A^T)=4 \\neq 16.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n3\\textrm{det}(A^T)= 3 \\cdot 4 = 12.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\textrm{det}(A^T)+\\textrm{det}(I)= 4 + 1 = 5 \\neq 17.\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119429 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3118d2af-771f-54c9-b18e-5196b87b6dca" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Volume of an N-Dimensional Parallelepiped"}] :question/id #uuid "a67e620f-6380-5754-81db-7e593cdf4336" :question/math-academy-id "e-10998" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043085/assets/47850d3c530a29de8cb5df4bb3e035b9e29fb1ba65ff0eca2d39e6d8e0a2b06b.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, let's construct the matrix $M,$ whose columns are the coordinates of our vectors $\\mathbf{a},$ $\\mathbf{b},$ $\\mathbf{c},$ and  $\\mathbf{d}{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043085/assets/0563d565dff1928d21da21ad832fad37f94fb385ddb8a805423ae2577ae9434c.png)\n\nThe volume of the parallelepiped spanned by these vectors equals the absolute value of the determinant of $M{:}$\n\n$$\nV = | \\det(M) |\n$$\n\nNotice that the $2$nd row of the determinant contains three zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $2$nd row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -4 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3|\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the $2$nd row of the $3 \\times 3$ determinant contains two zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $2$nd row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =-3|\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3\\cdot 1\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3(15+4) \\\\  & =-57.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume is\n\n$$\nV = | \\det(M) | = |-57| = 57.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186318707 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "02e65c73-8c02-5403-8c5c-b1e81f81a7b6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With Many Zeros"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47eb2c69-1413-513a-b390-8f44c6607b84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318709} {:answer/id #uuid "ed08d8bb-424c-56c8-9f8a-3354e28cc0cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318710} {:answer/id #uuid "7788f4d9-25a8-5ad7-95b0-1a6d93e2537d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318711} {:answer/id #uuid "fd7c8c9b-a40b-5ced-8c20-7de46d6d90c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318712} {:answer/id #uuid "9e2b317f-a93c-5e7e-aa47-e6c3d41bd083" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e2b317f-a93c-5e7e-aa47-e6c3d41bd083" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318713} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fc96394-b747-54f9-8d1e-5b34af8e98dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318708}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bc7bb8a5-4e30-5286-a345-3410950b7e92" :question/math-academy-id "q-130292" :question/problem "Find the determinant of the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the $3$rd column contains three zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $3$rd column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =2\\cdot 5\\cdot 6\\cdot (-1)=-60.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\ndet(B)=-60.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120080 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3118d2af-771f-54c9-b18e-5196b87b6dca" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Volume of an N-Dimensional Parallelepiped"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b029811e-e879-50d4-b3e4-9425ea62c0c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117046} {:answer/id #uuid "1732c718-7de5-5a3b-b424-697f9044d394" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117047} {:answer/id #uuid "1a51a659-d4b0-503c-86eb-d3bedf1e8356" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117048} {:answer/id #uuid "25f8124e-095f-524b-a1fd-0ef2bcae46c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117049} {:answer/id #uuid "5e0f1f54-7e26-512d-9f78-7d62fd2164d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117050}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25f8124e-095f-524b-a1fd-0ef2bcae46c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117049} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a160d73-5759-5492-b5ba-45edea0a6043" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117045}] :question/id #uuid "302209ad-3d64-52f9-9fa9-99104ad6beb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-157695" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$a = \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}, b = \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}, c = \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}, d = \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186318749 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3118d2af-771f-54c9-b18e-5196b87b6dca" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Volume of an N-Dimensional Parallelepiped"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9a432ef-750f-56e3-8b09-eee2e1fdf71c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "93" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318751} {:answer/id #uuid "bdaf7c33-f8dd-5a6a-8d55-c29e9565a104" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "81" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318752} {:answer/id #uuid "5f9159db-ef1b-5abb-8793-2add85297585" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "112" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318753} {:answer/id #uuid "b72e5390-ccf0-53c2-9796-4ecaa37c7e1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318754} {:answer/id #uuid "2b5dc6e5-7a99-5be8-a45d-96919f9d88e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "105" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318755}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b5dc6e5-7a99-5be8-a45d-96919f9d88e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "105" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318755} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d9a08a9-4553-597b-87e6-d1082c3b3862" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318750}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3d56fcd6-6f95-540c-9c10-601dc787ed40" :question/math-academy-id "q-158108" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$$\na=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,c=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,d=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's construct the matrix $M,$ whose columns are the coordinates of our vectors $a,$ $b,$ $c,$ and  $d:$\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 4 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe volume of the parallelepiped spanned by these vectors equals the absolute value of the determinant of $M:$\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. So, we have\n\n$$\ndet(M)=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 4 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}]=7\\cdot 3\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 5=-105.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume is\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|=|-105|=105.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120356 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "02e65c73-8c02-5403-8c5c-b1e81f81a7b6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With Many Zeros"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de9afb95-92b4-5593-8bb3-50131c4ee6c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118612} {:answer/id #uuid "1bfb9360-2c42-5633-af26-04085bb695c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118613} {:answer/id #uuid "23089ac5-199a-52d0-bce7-5fcb40214051" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118614} {:answer/id #uuid "3d7d491a-e852-58e0-a72c-4b12faa486ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118615} {:answer/id #uuid "49692b72-ff54-5c10-838c-cd04484f14e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118616}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d7d491a-e852-58e0-a72c-4b12faa486ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118615} :answer-field/id #uuid "2718242c-5cd5-5d5b-9cb3-d2a3d667291c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118611}] :question/id #uuid "1a43a5f7-bf85-5fa1-b02e-c33727064a7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-42472" :question/problem "Find the determinant of the matrix\n\n$B = \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 11 & 1 & 19 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186318812 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "02e65c73-8c02-5403-8c5c-b1e81f81a7b6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With Many Zeros"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "071ad2b8-d296-52de-a0ed-5b8d876b9ce8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318814} {:answer/id #uuid "50f9d3ad-bfad-5817-8640-f48fb154ed9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318815} {:answer/id #uuid "958992a9-ba88-55ea-a4e9-d153550bf044" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318816} {:answer/id #uuid "8e49e8c9-cb85-5740-b117-214bb26c1adc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318817} {:answer/id #uuid "1afedeca-3d90-5b13-84f1-8788735547d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318818}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e49e8c9-cb85-5740-b117-214bb26c1adc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318817} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef00e8eb-fb0e-510e-a1ab-788708341000" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318813}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e6db9f45-0830-59a7-8ba3-31125259ec1c" :question/math-academy-id "q-69979" :question/problem "Find the determinant of the matrix \n$G=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 13 & 6 & 7 & -2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the $4$th column contains three zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $4$th column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(G) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 13 & 6 & 7 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot (-1)^{4+4}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =(-2)\\cdot (1\\cdot 2\\cdot (-1))=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\ndet(G)=4.\n$$"}]}
